  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1117 AM MDT Mon May 11 2026\n\nVery little change from previous forecast packages with generally \ndry weather conditions and above average temperatures through the \nperiod.\n\n...TODAY THROUGH FRIDAY...\n\nUpper level ridge of high pressure will continue to slowly drift \neast across the Desert Southwest, and eventually over New Mexico. In \nresponse, surface pressure gradient will relax and lead to light \nafternoon winds through Wednesday. Also, as 500mb heights continue \nto rise, temperatures will also respond warming into the middle 90s \nwith middle to upper 90s on Wednesday and Thursday. Upper level \nPacific storm system coming onshore over NorCal on Wednesday and \nThursday will begin breaking down the aforementioned upper high as \nit slowly translates east. Modest moisture will lift north out of \nMexico ahead of the aforementioned system. Minor changes were made \nin the PoP and WX grids, I added 15 percent PoPs during the \nWednesday afternoon timeframe for eastern portions of the Gila \nRegion.\n\nUpper level system will move west to east well north of the forecast \narea with breezy winds returning on Thursday and Friday timeframe. \nTemperatures will remain in the 90s across the desert lowlands.\n\n...WEEKEND...\n\nBy this weekend, weak and baggy flow aloft will take control with \nlittle to no impacts to sensible weather conditions. Winds will \nremain light to low-end breezy with above average temperatures \ncontinuing.",
